The public repo search did not expose a canonical Phase 3 definition, so I made the next architectural step explicit rather than inventing a supposed existing repo definition.

The runtime actually executed. It completed its demo mission in 9 steps, produced 18 hashed ledger events, stored 8 Pattern Book records, learned 2 Metamap route priors, stayed inside its cost budget, and verified its ledger chain successfully. All 5 tests passed.

