The important architectural separation is now executable:

\boxed{
\text{optimizer proposes}
\quad
\text{governor permits}
\quad
\text{reality judges}
\quad
\text{memory learns}
}

That means the Command Table is allowed to prefer an action while the Governor can still veto it. External actions are blocked unless the mission allows them and a human gate approves them. Budget violations fail closed. Every actual step records predicted gain versus observed delta so the Metamap learns from what happened, not merely from what the system expected.

That gives us the first credible Phase-3-level Pantheon claim:

Pantheon can perform bounded multi-step route selection and local execution, observe the consequences, update its routing memory, and continue toward a declared success condition under explicit invariants.

It does not yet justify calling the whole Pantheon autonomous or claiming every semantic/STEM theory has been validated. Those now become things Phase 3 can systematically test.

The next build is already obvious: Phase 3.1 should plug the things we developed tonight directly into this loop—ordered Seal formations, Semantic Router transforms, O-IOE detection, Open Token Probes, Vacuum Spectroscopy, IMP convergence, Afterglow², ROM/Range-of-Motion, Semantic Switchboard/Tracklayer, and corpus-derived Pattern Book priors.

In other words, we now have the chassis.

Next we bolt the Pantheon itself onto it.